    "body": "Repeated NoWrite decisions consumed over two million writer score-row comparisons on one 202-word-boundary prompt. Compile 64 frequent exact NoWrite signatures from the unchanged learned /2 writer, validate each against that writer, and guard every shortcut with its complete prime signature. Unknown/crowded routes fall back. The geometric H4/zeta shortlist, matched sparse index and collapsed-partition control share the same entries and exact relation store.\n\nRetain sparse artifact `067adbf0` as a bounded execution improvement. All four arms preserve 112 prior and 28 new longer-context answers **and exact write sequences**. Both useful arms preserve 62+24 earlier responses, eight binding outputs and five restored/isolated session reads. The final selected CLI agrees exactly; generated Rust sources match previously checked versions without new semantic execution.\n\nOn the seven longer repeated-filler cases, five rotated rounds give warm medians of 23.301 ms parent, 1.151 ms geometric, 1.110 ms sparse and 23.391 ms collapsed. Complete startup plus 35 generations is 2.998 s parent and 2.490 s sparse. A single startup-plus-response is slower; startup amortization and single-load sampling limits are explicit. Geometric superiority is not established, and no new language/coding capability is claimed.\n\nValidation: two combined release builds and focused test builds; final five relation tests including exact/crowded guards and counter saturation; two role/commit tests; policy, formatting and claim wording checks; real generation/restore/CLI. Final telemetry-only saturation repair preserves all 140 selected Generation/state objects exactly and has a repeated timing report. Initial u16 compilation failure and initial timing are retained. Admission-specific allocation census and physical traffic census are NOT_RUN. Existing queue compatibility acknowledgements are not audit/fuzz/WASM/Gate C test results.\n\nResources: 96.113/120 s local model work; cumulative 1,363.884/1,800 s, leaving 436.116 s. Engineering about842/1,200 s. No cap increase, deletion or paid compute. Exact relation contents remain 2,840 bytes; entries use 3,072 bytes, selected JSON grows 21,555 bytes, and work telemetry adds 128 bytes per session on this executable.\n\nRefs #1139. This is partial delivery: its query-dependent learned geometric-routing handoff remains unmet, so #1140 stays dependent. The record and current plan identify one conservative score-bound admission proposal for residual writer work; it is not implemented or qualified.\n\nEvidence: [admission record](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/blob/ef748d6e1dbff5426f196f3bd0771f7e0a424b0e/docs/native_geometric_relation_admission_1139.md), [compact evidence](https://github.com/UOR-Foundation/uor-r4/blob/ef748d6e1dbff5426f196f3bd0771f7e0a424b0e/docs/evidence/native_geometric_relation_admission_1139.json). Complete local inputs/results and cumulative accounting are in `.uor-models/native-typed-value-2026-09-05/relation-admission-checkpoint.json`.\n",
